<name>Transmission/Transaxle</name>
<section id="1001Y_S000S" variety="S000S">
<name>CVT</name>
<ttl id="1001Y_S000S_744HD_T007Y" variety="T007Y">
<name>CVT System [Super CVT-i] (K112/K112F)</name>
<para id="RM000000FUE00OX" category="C" type-id="303M7" name-id="3225A-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>P2767/61</dtccode>
<dtcname>Primary Sheave Speed Sensor Circuit</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000FUE00OX_01" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000047K00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The engine control computer detects the input shaft speed from the signal from the primary pulley speed sensor (NIN) and performs shift control.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.18in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.90in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
<ptxt>1. Detection condition 2. Malfunction status 3. Malfunction duration 4. Other</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>P2767/61</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>While driving in the D position with output shaft speed of 300rpm or more (vehicle speed approximately 7km/h or more)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Primary pulley speed sensor speed is less than 300r/min</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Continuously for 2 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>1 trip</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Wire Harness and Connector</ptxt>
<ptxt>(NIN Sensor Signal System)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Transmission Revolution Sensor (NIN)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Engine Control Computer</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000FUE00OX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000047L00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C102334J13" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000FUE00OX_03" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000FUE00OX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___000047M00000">
<testtitle>Read TaSCAN Data (Primary Pulley Speed)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), display the [ECU Data Monitor] screen according to the screen display, and check the computer data.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>[Diagnosis menu screen: Powertrain → TCCS → ECU Data Monitor]</title>
<tgroup cols="4" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.60in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.33in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.58in"/>
<colspec colname="COL4" colwidth="1.57in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Item Name</ptxt>
<ptxt>[Symbol]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Item Description</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Reference Value</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Primary Pulley</ptxt>
<ptxt>Speed</ptxt>
<ptxt>[NIS]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Indicates primary pulley speed</ptxt>
<ptxt>Display Range: 0 to 12750rpm</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>When stopped</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>0rpm</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Primary Pulley</ptxt>
<ptxt>Speed</ptxt>
<ptxt>[NIS]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Indicates primary pulley speed</ptxt>
<ptxt>Display Range: 0 to 12750rpm</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Lock-up ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Same as engine speed</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>NG</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>OK</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0002" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0010" fin="false">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___000047N00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Transmission Revolution Sensor (NIN)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the transmission revolution sensor (NIN) connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C160034J03" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the connector terminals.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Name)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2(NIN+) - 1(NIN-)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>20°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>560 to 680Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0003" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0007" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___000047O00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Primary Pulley Speed Sensor (NIN) - Engine Control Computer)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the wire harness and connector inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the transmission revolution sensor (NIN) connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C159285J06" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect engine control computer connector A, and using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between each terminal. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000000FSD00RX"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Name)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A101(NIN+) - A102(NIN-)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>20°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>560 to 680Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0010" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0008" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0010" proc-id="RM0550J___0000BLJ00000">
<testtitle>Replace Engine Control Computer</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>For the replacement procedure, refer to <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000020V0005X"/></ptxt>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0005" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0005" proc-id="RM0550J___000047P00000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>TaSCAN (A/T / CVT Learned Value Initialization, G Sensor 0-point Learning and CVT Hydraulic Pressure Learning)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Initializing the learned values clears both the G sensor 0-point learning values and the CVT hydraulic pressure learning values, so when replacing the parts in the table below, perform AT/CVT learned value initialization and be sure to perform both G sensor 0-point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning.</ptxt>
<table>
<tgroup cols="1">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="4.13in"/>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry align="center">
<ptxt>Replacement Parts</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Continuously Variable Transaxle</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Engine Control Computer</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Skid control computer</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Oil Pressure Sensor</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Yaw Rate Sensor</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>After performing AT/CVT learned value initialization, be sure to perform G sensor 0-point learning first, and then CVT hydraulic pressure learning.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Be sure to place the vehicle on a level surface and perform 0 point learning.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Do not subject the vehicle to vibration while 0 point learning is in progress.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), perform A/T/CVT learned value initialization, G sensor 0 point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the procedures for A/T/CVT learned value initialization, G sensor 0-point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning, refer to <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000021F400AX"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the DTCs again. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000000FSM00TX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0009" fin="true">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0007">
<testtitle>Replace Transmission Revolution Sensor (NIN)</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000FUE00OX_04_0008">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Wire Harness or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
